lip during .omod extraction) is already fixed here: both\n36: \t   ModuleUtil.expandJar and ModuleUtil.expand reject entries that normalize outside\n37: \t   the target directory.\n38: \t   CVE-2026-40075 (ModuleResourcesServlet path traversal) is already fixed here:\n39: \t   ModuleResourcesServlet.getFile rejects paths that do not normalize within the\n40: \t   module resources base path.\n41: \t   CVE-2021-43094 (file exfiltration via /images and /initfilter/scripts) is already\n42: \t   fixed here: StartupFilter normalizes the resolved path and rejects requests that\n43: \t   resolve outside the served directory.\n44: \t   The remaining CVEs (CVE-2017-12796, CVE-2025-25928, CVE-2014-8073, CVE-2025-25927)\n45: \t   target the legacy admin UI / Reference Application (e.g. /admin/users/user.form),\n46: \t   which is not part of openmrs-core.\n47: \t   ]]></notes>\n48: \t   <cpe>cpe:2.3:a:openmrs:openmrs</cpe>\n49: \t   <cve>CVE-2026-40076</cve>\n50: \t   <cve>CVE-2026-40075</cve>\n51: \t   <cve>CVE-2021-43094</cve>\n52: \t   <cve>CVE-2017-12796</cve>\n53: \t   <cve>CVE-2025-25928</cve>\n54: \t   <cve>CVE-2014-8073</cve>\n55: \t   <cve>CVE-2025-25927</cve>\n56: \t</suppress>\n57: \t<suppress>\n58: \t   <notes><![CDATA[\n59: \t   False positive. Per the Apache advisory (GHSA-hf6x-8p5f-cgmf and the\n60: \t   oss-security announcement) both CVEs affect the 5.x artifact\n61: \t   org.apache.httpcomponents.core5:httpcore5 only (5.4.2 / 5.5-beta1 and\n62: \t   earlier); CVE-2026-54428 targets the HTTP/2 HPACK decoder, which the 4.x\n63: \t   line does not implement. We pull org.apache.httpcomponents:httpcore 4.4.16\n64: \t   transitively (hibernate-search elasticsearch rest4 client -> httpclient\n65: \t   4.5.14); 4.4.16 is the final 4.4.x release, so there is no 4.x upstream fix.\n66: \t   Dependency-Check matches it via the shared apache:httpcomponents_core CPE.\n67: \t   The regex is scoped to 4.4.x so a future move onto the affected 5.x line\n68: \t   would correctly 